3.5.2 Static Polymorphism
To illustrate the idea of static polymorphism, we consider the classic ex-
ample of clusters and partitions. As we mentioned before, a cluster is a group
of records, objects, or items. A partition of a dataset is a group of clusters.
Hence it is a good idea to write a container class that can hold different types
of data. The program shown in Listing 3.5 gives an example of a template
class Container.
